# DAAD Gathering schedule (this repo)

## What it is

Static **event schedule viewer** for **DAAD Gathering** (currently titled “2026” in `index.html`). Users browse lineup by day/stage, filter (date, stage, artist, tags, etc.), open sample-set links, and **download `.ics`** for selections or full schedule. No app backend in production: same behavior as **GitHub Pages** (HTML + client-side JS only).

## Stack & run locally

- **UI**: single-page `index.html` — Tailwind via CDN, custom “poster” CSS, Font Awesome, Google fonts (Barlow / Bebas Neue).
- **Companion page**: `downloads.html` (same visual language; downloads / links).
- **Dev server**: `server.py` — minimal `SimpleHTTPRequestHandler`, `/` → `index.html`, CORS `*` + no-store headers. Run: `python server.py` (default port **5500**).

## Data source (critical)

- Live schedule is loaded in the browser from a **public Google Spreadsheet** as CSV via the **GViz** endpoint:  
  `https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/{SPREADSHEET_ID}/gviz/tq?tqx=out:csv` (+ optional `&gid=`).  
  **Do not** switch to `/export?format=csv` for browser `fetch` — redirects break CORS on GitHub Pages.
- Constants in `index.html`: `SPREADSHEET_ID`, `SPREADSHEET_GID`, `EVENT_TIMEZONE` (`Europe/Budapest`), `DEFAULT_SLOT_HOURS` (default **2h** last slot on a stage/day).
- **`data/events.json`** / **`data/events_2025.json`**: legacy or snapshot data; **`fetchEvents()` does not load them** after the Sheet migration. Use/update the Sheet or adjust CSV parsing if the canonical source changes.
- **`ics/*.ics`**: bundled calendar files (older or partial exports); client-side **`generateIcsContent()`** in `index.html` is the in-app export path.

## Implementation map (`index.html` script)

| Concern | Functions / notes |
|--------|-------------------|
| Fetch + parse | `fetchScheduleCsvText`, `parseCsv`, `resolveColumnIndices` (headers: stage, band, date, time; optional tags; sample URL column matched with typo tolerance `samlpe`) |
| Times | `utcMillisForWallClock` / `toLocalIsoFromUtcMs` — wall-clock in `EVENT_TIMEZONE` |
| Stages | `normalizeStageName` → **uppercase** keys must align with **`STAGE_STYLES`** for colors |
| End times | `deriveEndsAndDuration` — next slot start per stage+day, else default duration |
| UI | Filter/render helpers, tag filter, cards with `sampleSetUrl`, loading overlay + error banner |

When adding stages or sheet columns, update **normalization**, **`STAGE_STYLES`**, and **CSV column resolution** together.
